{"id":"0d544339-3d6e-4e54-89ea-d813d6d9ca3d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7a58b186b6c963e7","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"af32d4e1bb078f75cb402211c8211ee7a83a0b18","start":5994,"end":6496},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","tagHit","(","callee",":","Tagged",",","site",":","HostCallSite",")",":","CapabilityHit","|","undefined","{","const","capability","=","callee","[","CAPABILITY","]",";","if","(","capability","===","undefined","||","!","ts",".","isCallExpression","(","site",".","node",")",")","{","return","undefined",";","}","const","argIndex","=","callee","[","RESOURCE_ARG","]","??","0",";","const","resource","=","site",".","args","[","argIndex","]",";","return","{","\"","capability","\"",":","capability",",","\"","resource","\"",":","typeof","resource","===","\"","string","\"","?","resource",":","\"","","\"",",","\"","callee","\"",":","renderCallee","(","site",".","node",".","expression",")",",","\"","dangerous","\"",":","isDangerous","(","capability",")",",","\"","argIndex","\"",":","argIndex","}",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"a0b013ea027c31e2","after":"1256159a477ece90"}},"payload":{"text":"Aliasing fallback: when AST classification misses (`const f = fetch; f(url)` — the callee is `f`), the invoked\nstand-in's own tag still identifies the capability. Same CapabilityHit shape as the shared AST classifier.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:01.296Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:01.296Z"}
{"id":"123cba7a-ba52-424a-850d-a498a754b59b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3cee79ee9c804a8d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7d02e10ff8a346c6e318d900a46b857e93b202f4","start":12614,"end":12636},"shape":{"type":"ObjectElement","atoms":["\"","maxSteps","\"",":","5_000_000",","]},"context":{"before":"dbb28dd598f10d72","after":"b698a6991d20b75d"}},"payload":{"text":"A fuel limit: this runs untrusted module code INSIDE the tsserver worker, so a `while (true)` must not\nhang the language server. Exceeding it throws uncatchably → caught below, partial observations kept.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:41.917Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:41.917Z"}
{"id":"194ef650-a606-4d1b-985f-61ef496d3bcc","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f0c12f04980c33b6","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0e877f4c984752a06691ecdfaab6cc6feaf22689","start":3404,"end":3457},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","LANDING","=","Symbol","(","\"","capabilities.canary.landing","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"fa0df61edb7d5524","after":"0f5c56d5e34db6d2"}},"payload":{"text":"A copy's or a rename's other path: what it does where it lands, its second argument (FS_DESTINATION).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:08.600Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:08.600Z"}
{"id":"1de9cdde-e66a-4789-be57-0d45731a3f9e","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8131ee7f8f9f05e8#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f6116587f90a69491cee727a89f7e6762a9ef253","start":2193,"end":2214},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","capability","\"",":","string",";"]},"context":{"before":"2cbcdf25b5bf3182#0","after":"1b6c0eb424c98528"}},"payload":{"text":"Capability class (silo vocabulary): net / fs:read / fs:write / exec.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:32.216Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:32.216Z"}
{"id":"20cd2ce2-36be-41df-8249-8cbdaf884d22","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a7e505d6860a4c71","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e1ad7c039e87e3c2ed854bbfc10f4631d5cf1435","start":0,"end":57},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","HostCallSite","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/tsval","\""]},"context":{"after":"1c1ec76d263966ed"}},"payload":{"text":"Capabilities canary — the DYNAMIC half of the capability IDE (the middle column: concrete pre-call values).\n\nThe static engine (engine.ts, util/silo `findReach`) captures a capability call's resource only when it's a\nSTATIC STRING LITERAL. The canary covers the rest: it RUNS the module in the tsval interpreter and, at the\nhost↔guest boundary, observes the CONCRETE argument each capability call is actually invoked with — the real\nURL a `fetch(base + id)` builds, the path a computed `writeFile(dir + name)` writes.\n\nThe interpreter IS the sandbox: tsval runs with zero ambient authority (no real fetch/fs/exec unless injected),\nand `HostGuard.beforeCall` fires BEFORE any host call, so nothing dangerous can execute — we observe and hand\nback an inert stand-in. That's why the canary needs no almostnode-style runtime: almostnode performs REAL\neffects (real network), the opposite of what a canary wants. `beforeCall` gives the call-expression node (→\nsource span, the same anchor the static rows use) and the arguments AS EVALUATED. Capability calls are\nclassified by the IDENTITY of the injected stand-in (each is tagged), which also catches aliasing\n(`const f = fetch; f(url)`); danger grading stays with silo policy (`isDangerous`, parser-free).\n\nThis runs INSIDE the tsserver plugin, reusing tsserver's own `typescript` (the build externalizes it), so the\nengine ships ~1MB instead of bundling a ~7MB copy. A step budget bounds the run so untrusted code can't hang\nthe language server. M0 scope: CALL capabilities that execute during a normal run (top-level, or reachable from\none); `env` is a member read the static half already resolves, so the canary skips it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:34.596Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:34.596Z"}
{"id":"32454413-91c1-415d-865f-8a5ad7febb82","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1191ea6be5d75b17","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"bf656325dc8a03e003ecb43e36fcbafc2c1afac1","start":7022,"end":7559},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","inert","(",")",":","unknown","{","function","target","(",")",":","void","{","}","return","new","Proxy","(","target",",","{","\"","get","\"",":","(","_target",",","property",")","=>","{","if","(","property","===","\"","then","\"",")","{","return","undefined",";","}","if","(","property","===","Symbol",".","iterator",")","{","return","function","*","(",")","{","}",";","}","if","(","property","===","Symbol",".","toPrimitive","||","property","===","\"","toString","\"","||","property","===","\"","valueOf","\"",")","{","return","(",")","=>","\"","","\"",";","}","return","inert","(",")",";","}",",","\"","apply","\"",":","(",")","=>","inert","(",")",",","\"","construct","\"",":","(",")","=>","inert","(",")","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"1256159a477ece90","after":"402a4138a833947a"}},"payload":{"text":"A recursive inert stand-in for an UNMOCKED module, so `import x from \"some-lib\"` (or `require`) doesn't abort the\nrun — the code keeps going and can still reach the capability calls it makes directly. Callable, constructable,\nevery property yields another inert; it deliberately does NOT look like a Promise (`then` undefined) and iterates\nas empty, so `await`/destructuring/`for…of` don't hang or throw. Untagged: unmocked modules aren't classified\n(a future refinement can tag known HTTP clients like axios); this is purely about not stopping the run.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:56.554Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:56.554Z"}
{"id":"62769a78-7911-4f60-ae4f-f179ac84be88","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"60a815d57c38a09f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"2e4f9d7f833a8a0136c6cf995435eac173c3e780","start":8721,"end":8900},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","fsResults",":","Record","<","string",",","(",")","=>","unknown",">","=","{","\"","readdir","\"",":","(",")","=>","[","]",",","\"","readdirSync","\"",":","(",")","=>","[","]",",","\"","existsSync","\"",":","(",")","=>","false",",","\"","createReadStream","\"",":","inert",",","\"","createWriteStream","\"",":","inert","}"]},"context":{"before":"81a36a4bc098d40d","after":"f28a03c0a96dedce"}},"payload":{"text":"Every method almostnode gates, as an inert stand-in: reads find nothing, writes (a copy or a rename's too) do nothing.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:51.664Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:51.664Z"}
{"id":"636ab519-fad8-47f1-9d9f-3bb4bed3d3bf","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b22366b560f05717","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/canary.ts","baseline":{"blob":"3def4a9ea38ece97785d341d6e9c38da3dbd78a9","start":11498,"end":11551},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","classified","=","classifyCall","(","site",".","node",",","site",".","args",")"]},"context":{"before":"84a52ed0bff42265","after":"fd5cdfbf067ddd88"}},"payload":{"text":"One classifier for everyone: the shared AST classifier decides capability + resource-arg; the tag is only\na fallback for aliasing the AST can't see. (The debugger uses classifyCall alone — it has no tags.)\n(a copy or a rename: one observation per path it reaches)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:44.324Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:57:44.324Z"}
